  "summary": "Idealized rural domesticity: baking, gardening, linen dresses and pastoral calm, amplified by pandemic-era escapism.",
  "description": "Cottagecore romanticizes agrarian life — sourdough, jam shelves, meadow picnics, hand-sewn linen — drawing on Beatrix Potter, BBC period dramas and pastoral tradition. It surged on Tumblr (2018), exploded during 2020 lockdowns (bread-baking, Taylor Swift's folklore), and intersects with LGBTQ+ community meaning-making. Critics note its erasure of actual rural labor; scholars treat it as digital pastoralism. Sub-branches: goblincore, fairycore, grandmillennial décor overlaps.",
